+name: autonoma
+repo: https://github.com/JoeisEvil/autonoma
+sha: 01cfc58ac9ee6dbcbe8633284c34aca700894ef0
+version: "0.1.0"
+description: "Earned autonomy: a trust score per kind of action (file edits, deletes, git push, network, messages, spending, system) that rises with clean work and falls on denials, corrections and failures. Below a class's threshold the call goes through Hermes's own approval prompt; at or above, it runs without asking. Catches the agent routing around a block (shell redirects, inline python/node code, `bash -c`), asks again for risky actions after the turn read outside content, revokes \"session\"/\"always\" grants after a correction, writes handoff notes from the tool log when a session ends unfinished, and adds a live dashboard tab. Disclosure — stores tool names, action classes, hashed arguments, file paths, command verbs, host names, short error excerpts and short excerpts of your messages and the agent's last reply (up to 500 characters) locally in <HERMES_HOME>/plugin-data/autonoma/data.db (90-day retention, configurable); injects a handoff note into the first turn after an unfinished session and a progress list after compaction; can raise Hermes approval prompts for actions below their trust threshold or after outside content and, when hard_floor_enabled is on, block a class for a number of turns after a correction; the dashboard tab's local routes read the ledger and can reset, set or freeze scores; makes no network calls, no telemetry, reads no credentials; optional corrections_llm (off by default) sends the previous assistant message and current user message to the active model to confirm a correction."
+maintainer: JoeisEvil
+tier: community
+category: tools
+requires_hermes: ">=0.23.0"
+docs_url: https://github.com/JoeisEvil/autonoma#readme
+image: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JoeisEvil/autonoma/56653cced2b4431db3c08dc680ccb5e139b6f125/docs/banner.jpg
