-description: "Your agent speaks and listens with Fish Audio: expressive voices in 80+ languages, voices you design from a sentence, and live word-by-word dictation. The official Fish Audio plugin: Fish's Drama 3 model with word-level direction, speech-to-text, Fish Audio's community voice library, voice cloning and voice design, with a Voices page in Hermes Desktop. Fish Audio becomes a Hermes speech and transcription provider for voice replies, read-aloud, voice notes and Desktop dictation, with sentence-by-sentence streaming in CLI voice mode and Desktop, and word-by-word live dictation captions on Hermes 0.21.6+ (stt.streaming: true). Adds the fish_speak, fish_voices, fish_transcribe, fish_settings, fish_account and fish_pronunciations tools, /fish and hermes fish commands (including /fish setup, a checklist that ends by offering a spoken sample with /fish preview), and four skills. Disclosure — sends your Fish API key and the text, audio (with file names) and voice titles, tags, descriptions, cover images and design instructions you ask it to process to api.fish.audio, or to the base_url you configure, and reads your Fish wallet for balances and model choice; with live dictation on, microphone audio streams to Fish's native realtime speech-to-text at api.fish.audio (transcribe-stream-1, Preview) while you speak, billed $0.36 per hour of open session, per second, including silence; a session opens with the first audio and closes once Fish confirms the last words (the plugin stops waiting after 15 seconds), or 30 seconds after the last audio of a cancelled recording; if a live session fails or returns no text, Hermes transcribes the recording as a file instead, a separate billed request; the live_transcription: compat setting uses Fish's older realtime endpoint instead, billed per committed phrase rounded up to a second; synthesis, transcription, cloning and voice design are paid requests billed to your Fish account, except the free s2.1-pro-free model (free through 30 November 2026), whose requests Fish may use to improve its models; when no model is set and your Fish wallet shows no API credit, free credit or past top-up, the plugin uses that free model (allow_free_model: false turns this off). The key comes from the profile's secret scope (Hermes stores it in the profile .env; a single-profile install may also read FISH_API_KEY from the environment). Generated audio and subtitles are written to Hermes's audio cache; clone samples, cover images and recordings it uploads must be regular audio or image files, and Hermes config, secret and credential paths are refused. Cloning and deleting voices from chat or the model tools go through Hermes's approval gate and follow your approval settings. The Desktop Voices page and a Fish Audio settings page add gateway routes under /api/plugins/fish-audio/, behind the Hermes dashboard's existing authentication. On the Voices page, previews, clones and voice designs are billed; cloning a voice or saving a designed one creates a voice in your Fish account; cloning and deleting are confirmed on the page (a speaker-consent box, a typed voice name) instead of through Hermes's approval gate; and Use sets the profile's Fish voice, and its speech provider when none is set. The settings page, the /fish and hermes fish commands and the fish_settings tool can set or reset the profile's Fish model, voice and reading speed and save up to 50 voice names in the profile's config, so the agent can choose its own voice under the same rules; fish_pronunciations sends the pronunciation dictionary names, descriptions and rules you ask for to api.fish.audio (dictionary management is free; speech that uses a dictionary is billed as usual), can store up to three dictionary references as the profile's default in its config, and deleting a dictionary or a version goes through Hermes's approval gate; /fish setup lists what the profile still needs without a Fish call, and to tell whether a key was saved after the gateway started it checks whether the profile .env has a non-empty FISH_API_KEY line without reading the key out; /fish preview with no voice plays a short billed sample in the profile's voice; fish_account reads the Fish wallet like /fish balance and estimates costs from a dated price table without a network call; /fish use and hermes fish use also make Fish the speech provider when none is set, and given a voice title they search your own Fish voices for it, and hermes fish login sets the speech and transcription providers when they are unset or you confirm. Preview and design audio files are deleted from the gateway once returned; a design's audio is held in gateway memory so you can save it, until it is saved, a later design or save finds it over an hour old, or the gateway stops; clone uploads are deleted after the clone, or by the next upload once idle for 15 minutes. With a key set, Desktop reads your Fish wallet when an agent is selected and about every five minutes, for the status-bar credit; favourites stay in Desktop's plugin storage on that computer, and fetched previews stay in the window's memory until it closes. When you ask for a voice that fits the agent, the voice-studio skill reads the agent's SOUL.md or persona and sends Fish a one- or two-sentence voice description, never the whole persona. Includes a report-a-problem skill: when you report a problem with Fish Audio, the agent runs hermes fish doctor --no-synth, /fish status, hermes --version and hermes plugins list --json, reads recent Hermes log lines that mention Fish, searches this plugin's GitHub issues for a few key words, drafts a bug report and files it to this plugin's repository as a public GitHub issue or comment with your gh login only after you approve the exact text; reports leave out keys, credit amounts and voice ids not confirmed as public library voices, and security problems go to the repository's private advisory form instead. No telemetry."
