 description: "Read-only diagnostics for Hermes configuration: /hermes-doctor in-session and hermes guide in a terminal. Twelve read-only health checks (config, mcp, skills, commands, hooks, plugins, memories, sessions, storage, dashboard, update, gateway) and points to 32 troubleshooting skills, installed separately as a skills tap, for what the built-in doctor doesn't cover. Complements — never replaces — hermes doctor. Disclosure — reads config.yaml, SKILL.md frontmatter, skill bundles, plugin manifests, the shell-hooks allowlist and the built-in MEMORY.md/USER.md stores read-only (the report quotes short memory snippets); the sessions and gateway scopes read the tail of logs/agent.log read-only for runaway-session and gateway websocket-disconnect signatures (session ids, model names, token counts, disconnect peers and reasons appear in the report); the dashboard scope reads the Hermes package-manager toolchain facts, the checkout's Node lock pin and package.json engines, the web UI build record and security.allow_lazy_installs read-only, and never runs node or npm; the storage scope stats $HERMES_HOME/state.db for its size only (never opens it); the update scope reads the update-lock record in the co-located hermes-agent checkout under $HERMES_HOME and probes it — owner-PID liveness, then a brief lock acquisition it releases immediately, opening the lock file writable, with a read-only fallback for a root-owned lock on POSIX (writes no content, never deletes the lock); registers one read-only plugin skill, hermes-guide:start, listed in model sessions while the plugin is enabled; /hermes-doctor and hermes guide run hermes config path as a subprocess (argument list, no shell); the default hooks check reads hook configuration, consent state and the exec bit in-process and executes nothing, while hooks --deep runs hermes hooks doctor, which executes every approved shell hook once with a synthetic payload (--fast starts no subprocess and executes no hook); /hermes-doctor and hermes guide (except with --fast or --json) also run git ls-remote once per process against the plugin's GitHub repo to print a newer-release notice (no download, no local writes); with opt-in proactive: true it runs the checks (including the agent.log scan and the update-lock probe) in-process at each session start/end (no hooks executed, no subprocesses, no network). The 32 troubleshooting skills are not loaded by the plugin: they install separately from the repo as a skills tap, which this entry's pin does not cover."
