+description: "A bespoke chat workspace for Hermes Desktop and the Webapp: it takes over the app's home route and replaces it with a three-column page — a rail of bots (one row per profile, each with its own conversations), the conversation itself with folded reasoning and tool runs, and a right panel for files, previews and session detail. Bots can answer with a structured block that the thread draws as rich components (status cards, tables, checklists, approval prompts) instead of prose; slash commands, per-bot models and a settings page come with it, and media blocks render images, audio and video inline. Disclosure — takes over the Desktop/Webapp home route by default: opening home or a session from the native sidebar redirects into Hermes UI (a palette command turns this off). Its side panel previews files that replies name (MEDIA: lines, attached-image paths) by reading them through the plugin's own backend routes, which accept any path under the profile home or the user's home directory except core-refused and credential files (.env*, auth.json, config.yaml, credentials, webhook_subscriptions.json, private keys, .ssh/.aws/.gnupg, secrets, mcp-tokens and pairing folders); previews stay on the device. The bots rail reads each profile's state.db read-only, and the usage meter calls https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1/usage only when the active profile holds OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY, with the key kept server-side. No telemetry."
