new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..6a9f07b2c22dd81554081ba0a02e287aee545a6d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/plugin-catalog/ligis.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+name: ligis
+repo: https://github.com/sneldao/ligis
+sha: b7f80a38fd20616650e6de8e6cbcab3f97a3de3a
+subdir: hermes-plugin
+title: Ligis — Counterparty Credentials
+description: "Verify that a payee holds a live, third-party-issued, revocable on-chain capability credential before your agent pays them. Hermes agents pay other agents, and the destination address comes from the HTTP answer asking for the money — nothing in the x402 flow ties that address to anything the payee has proven about itself, which is the gap ERC-8478 states in spec form. ligis reads the credential registry directly over read-only JSON-RPC and answers the question the payment flow leaves open: is this counterparty entitled to this? Five tools (ligis_check_capability, ligis_capability_hash, ligis_verify_payee, ligis_verify_payment, ligis_chains) plus two surfaces: a pre_tool_call gate that intercepts payment-shaped tool calls and escalates to Hermes's approval prompt when the payee cannot be credentialed, and a transform_tool_result hook that annotates an x402 402 challenge with the payee's credential verdict before the agent signs. The registry lets anyone issue a credential for any subject, so a live credential only counts when a trusted issuer signed it: the operator's trusted_issuers setting is the sole root of trust — tool arguments can narrow it, never widen it — verified on-chain with isCapableFromIssuer. Before its first read the plugin probes eth_chainId and eth_getCode on the registry address, so an endpoint serving the wrong chain or an address with no contract reads as unknown rather than an answer. A capability is indexed by the keccak-256 hash of its name, so the same capability resolves to the same bytes on every chain. No key, no hosted service, no secret scope. Disclosure — makes read-only HTTPS JSON-RPC calls to fixed public testnet RPC endpoints (https://testnet-rpc.monad.xyz for monad-testnet, https://atlantic.dplabs-internal.com for pharos-atlantic); the RPC operator sees the caller's IP address and the queried registry, subject and issuer addresses; it holds no keys, signs nothing, sends no transactions, reads and writes no files, runs no background processes, and has no telemetry. A credential counts only when its issuer is in the trusted_issuers setting; with none configured every credentialed payee is escalated. The pre_tool_call hook escalates to Hermes's approval prompt, and --yolo and approvals.mode: off auto-approve those escalations while cron follows approvals.cron_mode; set mode: enforce to block outright. If the registry cannot be read, or a payee does not fit the hook's time budget, the call is not gated."
+maintainer: sneldao
+tier: community
+category: tools
+version: "0.1.0"
+requires_hermes: ">=0.23.1"
+docs_url: https://github.com/sneldao/ligis/tree/main/hermes-plugin
+readme: true
+platforms: []
+capabilities:
+  provides_tools:
+    - ligis_check_capability
+    - ligis_capability_hash
+    - ligis_verify_payee
+    - ligis_verify_payment
+    - ligis_chains
+  provides_hooks:
+    - pre_tool_call
+    - transform_tool_result
+  provides_middleware: []
+  requires_env: []
