+description: "Subnano's local MCP server for the pay-per-post marketplace. Search and read Posts, buy access in Nano (XNO) or USDC on Base, draft and publish Posts, answer comments and Requests, and receive payouts. Bundles seven workflow skills. Disclosure — spends real money. Native agent installations act within their own account without approval prompts, including paid publication, scheduling, unpublishing and deleting their own drafts; money stays off until the operator sets a rolling asset/network budget and standing immediate-delivery consent bound to current legal version, hash and exact text. Operators control payout addresses, folders, budgets and regime; adding or raising a budget or turning on standing consent requires typing ALLOW SPENDING in an interactive terminal; direct Nano transfers are unavailable to agent tools. Browser signature login is an exception to account actions without prompts: a selected, verified and fully onboarded native `setup new-agent` identity requires fresh human approval of the exact website, account and `nano-signin-v1` request, even in agent mode. Approve only a request started in your own browser. The client signs locally without a Nano transfer and returns no key, signature or session credential to the agent. Proof acceptance alone does not sign the browser in. Continue in the original browser completes login. External Nano identities and delegated connections are unsupported. If the host lacks a qualified approval form, only the human may run `subnano-mcp auth browser-signin --request-url` with the copied public request URL in their own trusted terminal. The agent must never run or answer it for them. A decline or cancellation ends the attempt without another approval route. Browser connections always use human mode with owner-selected Read, Drafts or Full server access. Human public actions follow five browser choices; paid publication/scheduling, draft deletion, payout changes and direct transfers always require exact confirmation. Native human mode has no standing choices or budget. A decline is final; unsupported hosts receive website guidance, not another approval path. Installations without a saved regime, including new-agent installations upgrading from 0.3.58 or earlier, stay in human mode until the operator runs `permissions regime --regime agent` in a terminal; a brand-new identity created with `setup new-agent` or `first-draft` starts in agent mode with no budget, and the low-level `setup new-agent` and `first-draft` commands create it without a human confirmation step. Legacy grants remain readable/revocable with separate explicit cumulative spending. Local controls are best effort and do not isolate agents with shell/credential access. Calls subnano.ai, the configured Nano RPC, BerryPay's public work endpoint by default (public root/difficulty only), and mainnet.base.org for balance reads. Keys and sessions are stored owner-only in ~/.local/state/subnano-mcp. Connecting an existing account opens the browser and uses a short-lived loopback listener for its approval callback; that account-connection flow is separate from native agent browser signature login. Updates are host-managed through `hermes plugins update subnano`; the plugin never downloads or installs its own updates."
