 resume and read the history of every session of the profile, and answers approval prompts by voice or by tapping the page's allow-once/session/always/deny buttons, where a single spoken approval word (including \"always\") or a short approval phrase such as \"go ahead\", \"sure\", \"yeah\" or \"allow\" (approve once) is sent as the reply, so a misheard word can approve a command; microphone audio and reply text go only to the VoiceManager server you set (VOICE_UNLEASHED_VOICEMANAGER_URL, bearer VOICE_UNLEASHED_VOICEMANAGER_TOKEN), and nothing is stored; it registers stream observers (on_stream_delta, on_stream_end, on_session_end), which makes Hermes use streaming requests on every surface, tool observers (pre_tool_call, post_tool_call) that run for every conversation and never block a call, and pre_llm_call, which adds one instruction only to a Desktop or Webapp chat that has voice on; it reads a few undocumented core helpers and the gateway's session DB read-only, so a Hermes release can break it; the Desktop half ships switched off."
