+name: wow-addon-forge
+title: WoW Addon Forge
+repo: https://github.com/SnoobieJunes/hermes-wow-plugin
+sha: dad15557926f077b49f348237eab33d8f5b38057
+version: "0.1.0"
+description: "Builds World of Warcraft: Forever (client 1.60.1, Interface 16001) addons that load and run, for players who are not programmers. Nine tools: wow_env (install/addon detection), wow_api (queryable index of the real client build's API, events and restrictions), wow_check (six-stage static + headless verification: TOC lint, Lua 5.1 syntax, global resolution, restricted/secret API rules, headless load in an embedded Lua 5.1 VM stub of the game, efficiency lints), wow_test (multi-client headless Lua test runner), wow_new (scaffolds an addon from tested building blocks: core, replicated record log, guild sync, trust, lazy Classic-theme window, Discord bridge), wow_install (installs after wow_check passes, with backup), wow_savedvars and wow_errors (read game data and in-game Lua errors back, via the bundled ForgeProbe companion addon), and wow_bridge (file-based Discord seam: pull an outbox, push an inbox, one /reload of latency each way). Ships Guildhall, a guild-management addon built entirely with these tools (board, calendar, a Marks currency earned automatically by playing, Discord mirror), the wow-addon-builder skill, /wow, hermes wow, and an Addon Forge Desktop pane. Disclosure — runs addon and test Lua code you point it at inside an embedded Lua 5.1 VM (lupa, a native extension) on your machine; `wow_api sync` downloads public API documentation from raw.githubusercontent.com; reads your WoW install (Interface/AddOns, WTF SavedVariables, .build.info); `wow_install` replaces Interface/AddOns/<name> after backing the old folder up under the Hermes cache, `wow_bridge push` rewrites that addon's Inbox.lua, and `wow_new` creates a new addon folder at the path given."
+maintainer: SnoobieJunes
+tier: community
+category: general
+docs_url: https://github.com/SnoobieJunes/hermes-wow-plugin
+requires_hermes: ">=0.22.0"
